Verdict: NEED_MORE
Rationale: The claim has two parts: (1) the car that replaced the Type F129 (F355) was itself replaced by the F430, both by the company whose cars Vittorio Colocci raced; and (2) that car competed in the new Australian Nations Cup Championship in 2000. The evidence supports that the F355 was replaced by the Ferrari 360, not the F430, contradicting the first part. The evidence also shows the F430 was replaced by the Ferrari California, but no evidence confirms Vittorio Colocci raced either the F430 or the California. Additionally, there is no evidence confirming the California competed in the 2000 Australian Nations Cup Championship. Therefore, the claim is insufficiently supported and requires more evidence.
Rounds: 6, findings: 12
